{"slug":"/students/subjects/chemistry/acids-bases/acids-bases-intro/","source":"students/subjects/chemistry/acids-bases/acids-bases-intro.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Acids, Bases & Salts — Introduction","description":"","subject":"chemistry","body":"<div class=\"max-w-4xl mx-auto\">\n    <nav class=\"mb-4\">\n      <a href=\"/students/subjects/chemistry/acids-bases/\" class=\"text-emerald-600 hover:text-emerald-800 transition\">\n        <span class=\"mi -arrow-left mr-2\" data-mi=\"arrow_back\">arrow_back</span>Back to Acids &amp; Bases\n      </a>\n    </nav>\n    \n    <article class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-6 md:p-8 shadow-lg\">\n      <!-- Header -->\n      <div class=\"border-b pb-4 mb-6\">\n        <h1 class=\"text-2xl md:text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2\">\n          <span class=\"mi -flask text-purple-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"science\">science</span>Acids, Bases and Salts\n        </h1>\n        <p class=\"text-gray-600\">Understanding the fundamental concepts of acids, bases, and the salts they produce.</p>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Learning Objectives -->\n      <div class=\"bg-purple-50 border-l-4 border-purple-500 p-4 rounded-r-lg mb-6\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-2\"><span class=\"mi -bullseye mr-2\" data-mi=\"adjust\">adjust</span>Learning Objectives</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-1\">\n          <li>• Define acids and bases using different theories</li>\n          <li>• Identify properties of acids and bases</li>\n          <li>• Describe the pH scale and its significance</li>\n          <li>• Explain neutralization reactions</li>\n          <li>• Classify different types of salts</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n\n      <!-- Section 1: Definitions -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">1</span>\n          Definitions of Acids and Bases\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <!-- Arrhenius Theory -->\n          <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -user text-blue-500 mr-2\" data-mi=\"person\">person</span>Arrhenius Theory (1884)\n            </h3>\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n              <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-red-800 mb-2\">Acid</p>\n                <p class=\"text-red-700 text-sm\">A substance that produces <strong>H<sup>+</sup></strong> ions (protons) when dissolved in water.</p>\n                <p class=\"text-xs text-red-600 mt-2\">Example: HCl → H<sup>+</sup> + Cl<sup>-</sup></p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-blue-800 mb-2\">Base</p>\n                <p class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm\">A substance that produces <strong>OH<sup>-</sup></strong> ions (hydroxide ions) when dissolved in water.</p>\n                <p class=\"text-xs text-blue-600 mt-2\">Example: NaOH → Na<sup>+</sup> + OH<sup>-</sup></p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-yellow-700 text-sm mt-3 bg-yellow-50 p-2 rounded\"><strong>Limitation:</strong> Only applies to aqueous solutions; cannot explain basicity of NH₃.</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <!-- Brønsted-Lowry Theory -->\n          <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-3 flex items-center\">\n              <span class=\"mi -users text-green-500 mr-2\" data-mi=\"group\">group</span>Brønsted-Lowry Theory (1923)\n            </h3>\n            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n              <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-red-800 mb-2\">Acid</p>\n                <p class=\"text-red-700 text-sm\">A <strong>proton donor</strong> (H<sup>+</sup> donor)</p>\n                <p class=\"text-xs text-red-600 mt-2\">Example: HCl + H₂O → H₃O<sup>+</sup> + Cl<sup>-</sup></p>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-blue-800 mb-2\">Base</p>\n                <p class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm\">A <strong>proton acceptor</strong> (H<sup>+</sup> acceptor)</p>\n                <p class=\"text-xs text-blue-600 mt-2\">Example: NH₃ + H₂O ⇌ NH₄<sup>+</sup> + OH<sup>-</sup></p>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n            <p class=\"text-green-700 text-sm mt-3 bg-green-50 p-2 rounded\"><strong>Advantage:</strong> Explains basicity of ammonia and applies to non-aqueous solutions.</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 2: Properties -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">2</span>\n          Properties of Acids and Bases\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n          <!-- Acids -->\n          <div class=\"bg-red-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-red-200\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-red-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -tint mr-2\" data-mi=\"water_drop\">water_drop</span>Properties of Acids</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-red-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• Sour taste (e.g., lemon juice, vinegar)</li>\n              <li>• Turn blue litmus paper <strong class=\"text-red-600\">RED</strong></li>\n              <li>• React with metals to produce hydrogen gas</li>\n              <li>• React with carbonates to produce CO₂</li>\n              <li>• Conduct electricity in solution</li>\n              <li>• pH value less than 7</li>\n              <li>• React with bases to form salt and water</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n          \n          <!-- Bases -->\n          <div class=\"bg-blue-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-blue-200\">\n            <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-blue-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -tint mr-2\" data-mi=\"water_drop\">water_drop</span>Properties of Bases</h3>\n            <ul class=\"text-blue-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n              <li>• Bitter taste (e.g., soap, baking soda)</li>\n              <li>• Turn red litmus paper <strong class=\"text-blue-600\">BLUE</strong></li>\n              <li>• Soapy/slippery feel</li>\n              <li>• React with acids to form salt and water</li>\n              <li>• Conduct electricity in solution</li>\n              <li>• pH value greater than 7</li>\n              <li>• Can neutralize acids</li>\n            </ul>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 3: The pH Scale -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">3</span>\n          The pH Scale\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">The <strong class=\"text-purple-600\">pH scale</strong> is a measure of the acidity or alkalinity of a solution. It ranges from 0 to 14, with 7 being neutral.</p>\n          \n          <!-- Visual pH Scale -->\n          <div class=\"mb-4\">\n            <div class=\"ph-scale h-8 rounded-lg mb-2\"></div>\n            <div class=\"flex justify-between text-xs text-gray-600\">\n              <span>0 (Acidic)</span>\n              <span>7 (Neutral)</span>\n              <span>14 (Alkaline)</span>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border\">\n            <p class=\"font-mono text-center text-lg mb-2\">pH = -log[H<sup>+</sup>]</p>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600 text-center\">Lower pH = Higher [H<sup>+</sup>] = More acidic</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        \n        <!-- Common Substances Table -->\n        <div class=\"overflow-x-auto\">\n          <table class=\"w-full text-sm\">\n            <thead class=\"bg-purple-100\">\n              <tr>\n                <th class=\"p-3 text-left text-purple-800\">pH</th>\n                <th class=\"p-3 text-left text-purple-800\">Substance</th>\n                <th class=\"p-3 text-left text-purple-800\">Nature</th>\n              </tr>\n            </thead>\n            <tbody class=\"bg-white\">\n              <tr class=\"border-b bg-red-100\"><td class=\"p-3\">1</td><td class=\"p-3\">Stomach acid (HCl)</td><td class=\"p-3 text-red-700\">Strongly acidic</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-b bg-red-50\"><td class=\"p-3\">2-3</td><td class=\"p-3\">Lemon juice, vinegar</td><td class=\"p-3 text-red-600\">Acidic</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-b bg-orange-50\"><td class=\"p-3\">4-5</td><td class=\"p-3\">Tomatoes, coffee</td><td class=\"p-3 text-orange-600\">Weakly acidic</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-b bg-green-50\"><td class=\"p-3\">7</td><td class=\"p-3\">Pure water, blood</td><td class=\"p-3 text-green-600\">Neutral</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-b bg-blue-50\"><td class=\"p-3\">8-9</td><td class=\"p-3\">Baking soda, seawater</td><td class=\"p-3 text-blue-600\">Weakly basic</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"border-b bg-blue-100\"><td class=\"p-3\">10-11</td><td class=\"p-3\">Milk of magnesia</td><td class=\"p-3 text-blue-700\">Basic</td></tr>\n              <tr class=\"bg-indigo-100\"><td class=\"p-3\">13-14</td><td class=\"p-3\">NaOH, bleach</td><td class=\"p-3 text-indigo-700\">Strongly basic</td></tr>\n            </tbody>\n          </table>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 4: Neutralization -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">4</span>\n          Neutralization Reactions\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"bg-gray-50 p-5 rounded-lg mb-4\">\n          <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-3\"><strong class=\"text-purple-600\">Neutralization</strong> is the reaction between an acid and a base to form salt and water.</p>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-purple-200 text-center\">\n            <p class=\"text-purple-800 font-semibold mb-2\">General Equation:</p>\n            <p class=\"font-mono text-lg\">Acid + Base → Salt + Water</p>\n            <p class=\"font-mono text-lg mt-2 text-gray-700\">HCl + NaOH → NaCl + H₂O</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- Worked Examples -->\n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"border border-gray-200 rounded-lg overflow-hidden\">\n            <button class=\"accordion-btn w-full p-4 bg-purple-50 text-left font-semibold text-purple-800 flex justify-between items-center hover:bg-purple-100 transition\">\n              <span><span class=\"mi -lightbulb mr-2 text-yellow-500\" data-mi=\"lightbulb\">lightbulb</span>Worked Example 1: Writing Neutralization Equations</span>\n              <span class=\"mi -chevron-down transform transition-transform\" data-mi=\"expand_more\">expand_more</span>\n            </button>\n            <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n              <div class=\"p-5\">\n                <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Write the equation for the neutralization of sulfuric acid by potassium hydroxide.</p>\n                \n                <div class=\"space-y-3\">\n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 1:</strong> Write the formula of the acid and base</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-mono mt-1\">H₂SO₄ + KOH →</p>\n                  </div>\n                  \n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 2:</strong> Balance the equation (H₂SO₄ has 2 H⁺, KOH has 1 OH⁻)</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-mono mt-1\">H₂SO₄ + 2KOH →</p>\n                  </div>\n                  \n                  <div class=\"step-card bg-gray-50 p-3 rounded border-l-4 border-purple-500\">\n                    <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\"><strong>Step 3:</strong> Write the products (salt + water)</p>\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-700 font-mono mt-1\">H₂SO₄ + 2KOH → K₂SO₄ + 2H₂O</p>\n                  </div>\n                  \n                  <div class=\"bg-purple-100 p-3 rounded-lg\">\n                    <p class=\"text-purple-800 font-semibold\"><span class=\"mi -check-circle mr-2\" data-mi=\"check_circle\">check_circle</span>Answer: H₂SO₄ + 2KOH → K₂SO₄ + 2H₂O</p>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Section 5: Types of Salts -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"bg-purple-100 text-purple-700 w-8 h-8 rounded-full flex items-center justify-center mr-3 text-sm font-bold\">5</span>\n          Types of Salts\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Normal Salts</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Formed when all H⁺ ions of an acid are replaced. No replaceable H⁺ remains.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Examples: NaCl, K₂SO₄, CaCO₃</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Acid Salts</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Formed when only some H⁺ ions of a polyprotic acid are replaced.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Examples: NaHSO₄, NaHCO₃, KH₂PO₄</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Basic Salts</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Formed when not all OH⁻ ions of a base are replaced.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Examples: Pb(OH)Cl, Bi(OH)₂NO₃</p>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200\">\n            <h4 class=\"font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-2\">Double Salts</h4>\n            <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-600\">Contain two different cations in a definite proportion.</p>\n            <p class=\"text-xs text-gray-500 mt-1\">Examples: KAl(SO₄)₂·12H₂O (potash alum)</p>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Practice Problems -->\n      <section class=\"mb-8\">\n        <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4 flex items-center\">\n          <span class=\"mi -pencil-alt text-blue-600 mr-3\" data-mi=\"edit\">edit</span>\n          Practice Problems\n        </h2>\n        \n        <div class=\"space-y-4\">\n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">1. Define an acid according to Brønsted-Lowry theory.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>An acid is a proton (H⁺) donor.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">2. Write the balanced equation for the reaction between HNO₃ and Ca(OH)₂.</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>2HNO₃ + Ca(OH)₂ → Ca(NO₃)₂ + 2H₂O</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">3. Calculate the pH of a solution with [H⁺] = 0.01 mol/dm³</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>pH = -log[H⁺] = -log(0.01) = -log(10⁻²) = <strong>2</strong></p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n          \n          <div class=\"bg-yellow-50 p-4 rounded-lg border border-yellow-200\">\n            <p class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">4. Why is NaHCO₃ called an acid salt?</p>\n            <details class=\"mt-2\">\n              <summary class=\"text-sm text-blue-600 cursor-pointer hover:text-blue-800\">Show Answer</summary>\n              <div class=\"mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                <p>NaHCO₃ is an acid salt because it still contains one replaceable hydrogen ion (H⁺) from the parent acid H₂CO₃. It can further react with bases to form Na₂CO₃.</p>\n              </div>\n            </details>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </section>\n\n      <!-- Key Takeaways -->\n      <div class=\"bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-50 to-pink-50 p-5 rounded-lg border border-purple-200\">\n        <h3 class=\"font-semibold text-purple-800 mb-3\"><span class=\"mi -star mr-2\" data-mi=\"star\">star</span>Key Takeaways</h3>\n        <ul class=\"text-purple-700 text-sm space-y-2\">\n          <li>• Acids are proton donors (Brønsted-Lowry); bases are proton acceptors</li>\n          <li>• pH scale ranges from 0-14; pH 7 is neutral</li>\n          <li>• Neutralization: Acid + Base → Salt + Water</li>\n          <li>• Litmus is a common indicator: acids turn blue litmus red; bases turn red litmus blue</li>\n          <li>• Salts are classified as normal, acid, basic, or double salts</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n    </article>\n  </div>\n\n  \n\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-emerald-50 to-teal-100 p-4 md:p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body{font-family:Inter, sans-serif}\n    .content-card{backdrop-filter:blur(16px);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.95);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);box-shadow:0 8px 32px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);}\n    .accordion-content{max-height:0;overflow:hidden;transition:max-height 0.3s ease-out;}\n    .accordion-content.open{max-height:2000px;}\n    .step-card{transition:all 0.2s ease;}\n    .step-card:hover{transform:translateX(4px);}\n    .ph-scale{background:linear-gradient(to right,#ff4444,#ff8888,#ffffff,#8888ff,#4444ff);}"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}